@import url("unity-theme://default");

/* "Sunny Sticker", as in SMUP: chunky casual stickers. Everything has a thick navy outline, white or bright fills, round
   pills and rounded cards, and a hard navy drop under it, which UI Toolkit (no box-shadow) draws as a thicker bottom
   border that PillShape (Scripts/UI) redraws with the fill's bottom corners round. All text is Lilita One, a font asset
   made from the font in UI/Fonts, so display text can take an outline. The design is the Claude Design canvas
   "Toy Car Arena UI" (its stage sizes are the reference pixels used here).

   The palette, as variables every style sheet of the panel can use (var(--navy)). Translucent colours cannot be built
   from them, so they are written out where used: rgba(29, 43, 79, 0.6) dims a screen, 0.75 is a plate under white text.
   - navy: outlines, drops, text on white; white: cards, pills, text on the game
   - soft: a panel inside a card, a place past the podium, a white button's face under the pointer; shade: a white
     button's face shade; muted: captions and secondary text
   - red: the last seconds, a knock-out; gold: a win, first place, the stopwatch; silver, bronze: second and third place
   - green/green-shade/green-hover: the primary button
   - confetti: red, blue, green, orange, purple and gold
   - the cars' bodies (car-color in ui_screens): green, red, blue, gold, purple, orange, pink and charcoal, as CarLook
     paints them from the atlas */
:root {
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/UI/Fonts/font_lilita_one.asset");
    color: #1d2b4f;

    --navy: #1d2b4f;
    --white: #ffffff;
    --soft: #eef3fb;
    --shade: #c7d3ea;
    --muted: #5b6b8c;
    --red: #ff4d4d;
    --gold: #ffc93c;
    --silver: #b9c6d8;
    --bronze: #d98a4e;
    --green: #5bd34a;
    --green-shade: #2f9e2a;
    --green-hover: #74de63;
    --blue: #38b6ff;
    --orange: #ff9f1c;
    --purple: #b06cff;
    --pink: #ff7eb6;
    --charcoal: #4a5063;
}
